.TH true 1 "FUZIX System Utilities" "FUZIX"
.SH NAME
true, false \- exit with a fixed status
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B true
.br
.B false
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B true
does nothing and exits 0.
.B false
does nothing and exits 1.
.PP
They exist so that a shell script can say what it means:
.B while true
for a loop with no end, and
.B false
where a placeholder command has to fail.
.SH OPTIONS
None.  Arguments are ignored.
.SH NOTES
The shell has neither built in, so each one is a fork and an exec.  A
tight
.B while true
loop is more expensive here than it looks.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sh (1),
.BR test (1)
